          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            What is called
            %em Thom’s theorem
            or the
            %em Pontrjagin-Thom isomorphism
            (due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Thom54"} Thom 54
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Pontrjagin55"} Pontrjagin 55
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangential+structure"} tangential structure
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group+of+a+spectrum"} stable homotopy groups
            of the universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectrum"} ring spectrum
            structure, form the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+ring"} cobordism ring
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                    %mi G
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega^G_\bullet \simeq \pi_\bullet(M G)
          %p
            of manifolds with that
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangential+structure"} tangential structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            is exhibited by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin-Thom+construction"} Pontryagin-Thom construction
            (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "Pontrjagin-Thom+collapse+map#ForEmbeddingsIntoAnNSphere"} there
          %p
            More generally, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            = succeed "-bordism" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "-manifolds" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is isomorphic to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+homology"} generalized homology
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M G
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                    %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mi G
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi M
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega^G_\bullet(X)
                  \\simeq
                  \\pi_\bullet( M G \wedge X_+)
                  \\simeq
                  M G_\bullet(X)
          %h2#Ingredients Ingredients
          %h3#tangential_structure_on_the_stable_normal_bundle Tangential structure on the Stable normal bundle
          #ClassifyingMapOfNormalBundle.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              and equipped with an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding"} embedding
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i \;\colon\; X \hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}^k
            %p
              for some
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \mathbb{N}
              %strong classifying map of its normal bundle
              is the function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Gr
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi B
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo −
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    g_i \;\colon\; X \to Gr_{k-n}(\mathbb{R}^k) \hookrightarrow B O(k-n)
            %p
              which sends
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              to the normal of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+space"} tangent space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi x
                    %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi x
                    %mi X
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊥
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    N_x X = (T_x X)^{\perp} \hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}^k
            %p
              regarded as a point in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo −
                          %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_{k-n}(\mathbb{R}^k)
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+bundle"} normal bundle
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              itself is the subbundle of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi k
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi k
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    T \mathbb{R}^k \simeq \mathbb{R}^k \times \mathbb{R}^k
            %p
              consisting of those vectors which are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal"} orthogonal
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+vectors"} tangent vectors
              of
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi i
