            %p
              where the bottom morphism is the canonical inclusion (
              %a{:href => "classifying+space#InclusionOfBOnIntoBOnPlusOne"}> def.
              ).
            %p
              Now we claim that taking the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              in each of the four corners of this system of pullback diagrams yields again a pullback diagram, and this proves the claim.
            %p
              To see this, remember that we work in the category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{cg}
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#kTop"}> def.
              ). By their nature, we may test the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              of a would-be
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              space already by mapping
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+spaces"} compact topological spaces
              into it. Now observe that all the inclusion maps in the four corners of this system of diagrams are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+cell+complex"} relative cell complex
              inclusions, by prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CWComplexStructure"}
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#CompactSubsetsAreSmallInCellComplexes"} this lemma
          #UniversalThomSpectrum.num_defn
